  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "106",
  "quote": "A landlord may require a tenant to pay a rent deposit with respect to a tenancy if the landlord does so on or before entering into the tenancy agreement.",
  "reason": "Section 106 of the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 expressly permits a landlord to require a rent deposit of up to one month's rent on or before entering into the tenancy agreement, to be applied to the last rent period."
}

